Z||000000||saleenfiero||06-21-2001||10:39 PM||||This forum has and always will be a hotbed of valuable and useless info alike.  Anything you want to know about a fiero can be found here (except drex can't seem to get his sending unit question answered!)  <BR>Anywho, perhaps we should ask and answer the original questions posted by Clifford on the forum homepage:<P>How do we make our tires burn rubber?  Hmmmm<BR>How do we avoid speed traps?  Hmmm<BR>How do those other cars suck compared to the fiero?  Hmmmm||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-21-2001||11:56 PM||||Well to make my tires chirp I usually have to have<P>1.  A cool day and a very cool engine<P>2.  A fresh patch of asphalt, not old rough stuff<P>3.  Let out the clutch just right while stomping the gas.<P>4.  Or, I could just be turning real fast and <I>then</I> stomp on it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thats about the only way I can get my car to squeel.  I know all you V6 guys can get it no problem, but my car makes about <B><I>this</I></B> much horsepower *holding up thumb and forefinger*||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||06-22-2001||12:23 AM||||Well, for me to "chirp" or at least spin my tires it has to be raining and i have to be turning...then i can get them to make some noise and get the car sideways. <P>I avoid speed traps by not speeding!<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||1
